# Copy to .env. Both values come from Project Settings → API in Supabase.
#
# The anon key is public by design: it ships inside the app binary and is only
# useful in combination with row level security, which every table has
# (supabase/migrations/0005_rls.sql). The service-role key belongs nowhere near
# this project.
#
# Without this file Shift runs fully offline — workouts are logged to the local
# SQLite database, routine links still work, and the outbox simply never drains.
# That is a supported state, not a broken one. What needs a project: sync,
# squads, friends, and sending a routine to a friend (a routine *link* does not).

EXPO_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=https://your-project-ref.supabase.co
EXPO_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=your-anon-key
